{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>יכרסמנה</b> — A quadrilateral word like ירמסנה. And some say: a compound word — יכרת ממנה, in the manner of: מלא כרשו מעדני [content omitted, as it is a non-Hebrew phrase]. And this is far in my eyes." "<b>חזיר</b> — a beast." "<b>וזיז</b> — a bird, and it is a species name." "<b>ושדי</b> — like שדה; and the proof: יעלוז שדי וכל אשר בו (Job 41:12 [MT 41:20])." "And the meaning of חזיר — and bird — the nations, which are like beasts and birds of prey."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כדרך: מלא כרשו מעדני' appears to be a non-Hebrew (possibly Judeo-Arabic or Aramaic) proverb illustrating a compound word; rendered literally as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:37.316706188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}